-- title:
--   Overlap automorphisms realising a prescribed tangent cochain
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a local Artinian ring $B$ with algebraically closed residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,B$, and a $B$-algebra $B_1$ such that $B \to B_1$ is surjective with nilpotent kernel $J$ satisfying $J \cdot \mathfrak m_B = 0$ and $J \subseteq \mathfrak m_B$, and assume $q$ is nilpotent in $B$. Let $f_1 : A_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ carry a commutative relative group law $L_1$ together with the bundle of properties (smooth, proper, connected fibres, group law nonempty), let $F$ be a commutative formal group law in two variables over $B$ and $\theta_1$ a system of formal coordinates for $L_1$ with respect to $F \otimes_B B_1$; assume further that every point of $A_1$ over a $B_1$-algebra $C$ killed by some $q^m$ under iterated addition is infinitesimal along some nilpotent ideal of $C$, and that for every surjection $\rho : B \to k'$ onto a field the quotient of $k'[[x_1,x_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the $q$-th iterate series of $F \otimes_B k'$ has dimension $q^4$. Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space, also a $B$-module compatibly and with central opposite action, and $\iota : V \to B$ an injective $B$-linear map with image $J$. Let $D_0$ be a bare deformation of $(f_1, L_1)$ to $B$ — a scheme $D_0.A$ with structure map $D_0.f$ to $\operatorname{Spec} B$, a commutative relative group law $D_0.L$ with the abelian-scheme property bundle, and $D_0.g : A_1 \to D_0.A$ making the square over $B \to B_1$ cartesian and compatible with the group laws — with $D_0.f$ separated. Let $\mathcal U$ be a finite ordered affine cover of $D_0.A$ (affine opens $U_i$ indexed by a linearly ordered finite set, covering $D_0.A$), $i_0$ an index, $e_0$ a factorisation of the identity section of $D_0.L$ through $U_{i_0}$, and $e_1$ the corresponding factorisation of the identity section of the base-changed group law over $k$ through the $i_0$-th chart of the base-changed cover. For each overlap index $s$, that is each strictly increasing pair of indices with intersection $U_s = \mathcal U.\mathrm{inter}\,s$, let $\sigma_s : k \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, U_s) \cong \Gamma(A_k, U_{s,k})$ be a ring isomorphism compatible with pullback of sections along the first projection and with the $k$-algebra structures, where $A_k$ denotes the pullback of $D_0.f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} B$. Finally let $c$ be a $k$-linear point derivation of $\Gamma(A_k, U_{i_0,k})$ at the point determined by $e_1$ (i.e. $c(ab) = \mathrm{ev}(a)c(b) + \mathrm{ev}(b)c(a)$) with values in $\operatorname{Hom}_k(V^\vee, \check C^1(\mathcal U_k, \mathcal O))$, all of whose values are Čech $1$-cocycles. Then for every overlap index $s$ there is an isomorphism $\tau_s$ of the scheme $U_s$ with itself such that $\tau_s$ followed by the inclusion of $U_s$ and by $D_0.f$ equals the inclusion followed by $D_0.f$, and such that the restriction of $D_0.g$ to $U_s$ followed by $\tau_s$ equals that restriction, and there is a map $c_s : \Gamma(A_k, U_{i_0,k}) \to \operatorname{Hom}_k(V^\vee, k \otimes_B \Gamma(D_0.A, U_s))$ which is a system of tangent coordinates for the pair consisting of the canonical map $\operatorname{Spec}\Gamma(D_0.A, U_s) \to D_0.A$ and its twist by $\tau_s$, in the sense that there are a map from the spectrum of the thickening $(k \otimes_B \Gamma(U_s)) \otimes_k (k \oplus V)$ to $A_k$ realising that pair as a Schlessinger-type tangent vector along $J$ and $\iota$, a factorisation through the chart $U_{i_0,k}$ of its translate by the base-changed group law, and $c_s$ is the resulting tangent-coordinate function; moreover $\sigma_s(c_s(a)(\xi))$ equals the $s$-component of $c(a)(\xi)$ for all sections $a$ and all $\xi \in V^\vee$.
--
--   This is the chart-by-chart step in re-gluing a bare deformation along a prescribed tangent cochain: on each overlap of the ordered affine cover it produces an automorphism of the overlap, trivial over the base and over the closed fibre $A_1$, whose tangent coordinates match the given point derivation $c$ in that component. It feeds the construction of a deformation re-glued by $c$ in [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isRegluingBy_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isRegluingBy_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt), via the realisation of point derivations as tangent data over small extensions.
